\section{Validation}{

The statistic and its null variance are checked against an independent
reconstruction of Szroeter (1978) in
\file{tests/testthat/test-pass-a-reference.R}. Releases before 0.7.0 divided
the centred statistic by a further \eqn{\sqrt{n}}, shrinking \eqn{Q} by a
factor of roughly \eqn{2 / \sqrt{n}} and leaving the test with essentially no
power against any alternative; see \file{NEWS.md}.
}

\section{Supported models}{

It accepts an \code{lm} and a \code{glm} with the Gaussian family and the identity link,
unweighted or with positive weights, a \code{fitWLS()} fit and, since 0.16.0, a
rank-deficient fit, which it tests on the estimable part of its design: it gives
the value of the same model fitted without the aliased columns. It refuses a
\code{glm} of another family or link, a \code{survey::svyglm()} fit, a fit with a zero
weight, a coefficient that is not finite for another reason, and \code{data} that
lack rows or variables of the fit.
It refuses a multivariate \code{lm} ("needs a model with one response"), since
0.16.0; before, it stopped with a coercion error. An \code{mgcv::gam()} fit is
tested as before 0.16.0, with smooth terms too, until a later step settles
which tests take such a fit; since 0.16.0 its observations are matched to the
rows of \code{data} by the row names of its model frame. Before, they were matched
by position, since the residuals of a \code{gam} carry no names, and \code{data} with
the rows of the fit in another order gave a wrong value.
Which model each test accepts, and why, is set out in \code{\link{test_results}}, under
\emph{Supported models}.
}
\examples{
data(mtcars)
mod <- lm(mpg ~ wt + qsec, data = mtcars)
performSzroeterTest(mod, mtcars, order_by = "wt")

# Detect ordered heteroscedasticity in simulated data with variance increasing
# in an index variable
set.seed(404)
n <- 150
x <- sort(runif(n))
y <- 2 + 0.5 * x + rnorm(n, sd = 0.4 + 0.8 * x)
df <- data.frame(y, x)
performSzroeterTest(lm(y ~ x, data = df), df, order_by = "x")

# Two-sided version when the direction of the change is not known in advance
performSzroeterTest(mod, mtcars, order_by = "wt", alternative = "two.sided")

}
